For a set of molecules, the root mean square (rms) speed is

\[
v_{\text{rms}}=\sqrt{\frac{v_1^2+v_2^2}{2}}
\]

since there are two molecules.

Given:
\[
v_1=9\times 10^6\ \text{m/s}, \qquad v_2=1\times 10^6\ \text{m/s}
\]

Square them:

\[
v_1^2=(9\times 10^6)^2=81\times 10^{12}
\]
\[
v_2^2=(1\times 10^6)^2=1\times 10^{12}
\]

Average of squares:

\[
\frac{81\times 10^{12}+1\times 10^{12}}{2}
=\frac{82\times 10^{12}}{2}
=41\times 10^{12}
\]

Now take the square root:

\[
v_{\text{rms}}=\sqrt{41\times 10^{12}}
=\sqrt{41}\times 10^6
\approx 6.4\times 10^6\ \text{m/s}
\]

So the rms speed is about \(6.4\times 10^6\ \text{m/s}\).

